    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **255 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `customerCode` assignment for owners, formatted `<LAST3>-<NNNN>`.\n\n**What the rule does:** When an owner is created via `POST /api/owners`, they're assigned a `customerCode` where `LAST3` is the upper-cased first three letters of the last name and `NNNN` is a global 4-digit zero-padded sequence equal to one more than the current number of owners (e.g. `SMI-0007`).\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** (model) \u2014 added a persisted `customer_code` column with getter/setter.\n\n2. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 in `addOwner`, assign the code just before saving via a new `nextCustomerCode(lastName)` helper that computes `LAST3` and sequence = `clinicService.findAllOwners().size() + 1`, formatted with `String.format(\"%s-%04d\", ...)`. The count is read before the save, so each successive owner gets a consecutive number.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `customerCode` property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field and MapStruct maps it automatically onto the `GET /api/owners/{id}` response.\n\n4. **Schema DDL** \u2014 added the `customer_code` column to the `owners` table in all four dialects (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres); the test profile uses hsqldb with `ddl-auto=none`, so the schema change was required for the field to persist.\n\nThe `coreFormatAndGlobalSequence` acceptance test passes (verifying the `SMI-`/`JON-` prefixes and the consecutive global sequence), along with the entire existing suite.",
